# Monster Dialogue that feels hostile.
The monster stares into your soul. You feel a chill run down your spine.
Gurgling and growling, the monster seems to be sizing you up.
The monster's eyes narrow as it looks at you.
The monster snarls and bares its teeth.
The monster's eyes flash with anger.
Gurgle Gurgle
⟟ ⍙⟟⌰⌰ ☍⟟⌰⌰ ⊬⍜⎍
Growls echo from the depths, a warning of what lies below.
"Leave these waters," a voice hisses from the shadowy shallows.
The screech of something unseen, piercing the foggy night.
Claws scraping against hull, seeking entry to your sanctuary.
A deep, resonant bellow shakes the water around you.
Your presence disturbs the ancient one
A chorus of howls, the sea's monsters calling to one another.
Turn back, intruder
The sound of scales against rock, a serpentine creature approaches.
A hissing laughter, mocking your precarious situation.
Gurgling roars from below, a sign of displeasure from the deep.
Leave or perish
The crackling of tentacles, writhing in anticipation.
A low, menacing hum, the prelude to an attack.
The shriek of something vast, surfacing with hostile intent.
Slithering whispers, promising doom for the unwelcome.
A cacophony of clicks and tones, an aggressive underwater communication.
Your vessel trespasses sacred depths
The slap of heavy tails against water, a sign of approaching danger.
A thunderous growl, the ocean's depth voicing its anger.
None return from these cursed waters
An eerie silence, followed by a sudden, terrifying roar.